problem:
Prove that the fraction $(21n+4)/(14n+3)$ is irreducible for every natural number n.

proof:$gcd(21n+4, 14n+3) = 1$ then $2(21n+4) - 3(14n+3) = -1$, since the only postive number that divides -1 is 1 so the fraction cannot be reduced.\
*why $2(21n+4) - 3(14n+3) = -1$?*

